      "writtenOn": "2018-11-07T08:22:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is fair. The problem this fixes doesn\u0027t really cause any runtime issues, but if the prefetch happens to be near the end of the hashtree, we will do a lot of work for nothing and spam the kernel log with errors. This is not very likely to happen with /system, but pretty much guaranteed to happen with APEX modules, most of which are small and typically have a hashtree much smaller than the prefetch size.\n\nLet me know where you want this to go.",
